# Internationalization

Localize all static, application-owned user-facing text with `next-intl`. Never hardcode translatable UI strings.

Use `getTranslations` / `getFormatter` in Server Components and `useTranslations` / `useFormatter` in Client Components. Format user-facing dates, times, numbers, and currencies with next-intl formatters or ICU message formatting — not ad-hoc `toLocaleString` / manual string templates for display.

Reuse existing translation keys when appropriate. When adding copy, update the relevant locale files under `messages/` for every supported locale (`en`, `vi`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded UI string
<button>Save trip</button>

// ✅ GOOD — Server Component
import { getTranslations } from 'next-intl/server'

export default async function Page() {
  const t = await getTranslations('trips.create')
  return <button>{t('actions.publish')}</button>
}

// ✅ GOOD — Client Component + formatter
'use client'
import { useFormatter, useTranslations } from 'next-intl'

export function TripMeta({ date, budget }: Props) {
  const t = useTranslations('trips')
  const format = useFormatter()
  return (
    <p>
      {t('meta', {
        date: format.dateTime(date, { dateStyle: 'medium' }),
        budget: format.number(budget, { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD' }),
      })}
    </p>
  )
}
```

## Message key grouping

Organize keys in each `messages/{locale}/**/*.json` file into nested groups by purpose. Prefer a small set of shared group names so catalogs stay scannable and consistent across locales and features.

Common groups:

| Group | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `metadata` | Page / document title and description |
| `content` | Page chrome copy (eyebrow, title, intro, helper text) |
| `labels` | Field and section labels |
| `fields` | Form field names when distinct from labels |
| `placeholders` | Input placeholders |
| `actions` | Buttons, links, and other CTAs |
| `errors` | Validation and failure messages |
| `messages` | Transient status / loading copy |
| `prompts` | Short prompts (e.g. “New here?”) |
| `descriptions` | Longer helper or alt text |

Feature-specific groups (`steps`, `filters`, `status`, `itinerary`, …) are fine when they name a clear UI region. Keep leaf keys `camelCase`. Mirror the same nesting in every locale file.

Access nested keys with dotted paths (or a scoped namespace):

```tsx
const t = useTranslations('auth.login')
t('actions.submit')
t('errors.emailInvalid')
```

```json
// ❌ BAD — flat bag of unrelated keys
{
  "title": "Sign in",
  "submit": "Sign in",
  "emailInvalid": "Enter a valid email.",
  "passwordPlaceholder": "Enter your password"
}

// ✅ GOOD — grouped by purpose
{
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Sign in",
    "description": "Sign in to continue planning your journey."
  },
  "content": {
    "title": "Continue your journey"
  },
  "placeholders": {
    "password": "Enter your password"
  },
  "actions": {
    "submit": "Sign in"
  },
  "errors": {
    "emailInvalid": "Enter a valid email."
  }
}
```
